      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TEWKESBURY (2) has settled off the speed then worked home in good style in his two runs this prep, the latest over 2200m at the Sunshine Coast. Doesn't win too often but his third-up form reads well and in this company he looks ideally placed to score. CARACORON (1) overcame early interference to storm home and grab third last time out over 1526m at this track. Fitter for two runs back from a spell and he finds his best form when he gets out to this sort of journey. RIGHTEOUS (3) hasn't been far away at his last couple, most recently battling away gamely for fourth over 2200m at Grafton. Should be at his peak after four runs back from a lay-off. OUR SPARKY (6) won two in a row then didn't handle dropping back in distance last time in a run worth overlooking. On trial at this trip but can feature without surprising. SEERESS (8) failed at Eagle Farm last Saturday but can bounce back.",
